;; Every binary operator over TIME, DATE, TIMESTAMP and TIMESPAN against
;; each other and against I64, I32 and F64 (#1081), in atom, null-atom,
;; vector, vector-atom and select forms.  Generated from a differential
;; sweep against dev: only TIME +/- TIME and TIMESPAN, and TIME div, / and
;; xbar with a TIMESPAN, answer differently from dev.  Pins the rest so a
;; temporal rule cannot bleed into another operator unnoticed.  Temporal values
;; are compared as their I64 counts (large hours or years do not parse).
;;
;; Pairs whose vector and query forms already disagree on dev are listed at
;; the end and not pinned.

